      "prompt": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "A ball is launched into the air from the top of a building with a height of 50 feet. According to a\nquadratic model, 3 seconds after the ball is launched, it reaches its maximum height of 194 feet\nabove ground level. Which equation represents this model, where $h(t)$ is the ball’$s$ predicted\nheight, in feet, above ground level $t$ seconds after it was launched?"
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "kind": "editable-pdf-source",
        "sourceSetId": "pdf-3f20c3da269b45be902763524a375144",
        "sourceQuestionId": "m1-q10"
      },
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "choice-a",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "text": "$$h(t)=16t2+50$$"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "choice-b",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "text": "$$h(t)=-16t2+194$$"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "choice-c",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "text": "$$h(t)=-16t2+96t+50$$"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "choice-d",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "text": "$$h(t)=16t2-96t+194$$"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
